item.content:encoded:
&lt;p&gt;Si vous avez un projet Symfony récent, il y a de bonnes chances que vos icônes passent par &lt;a href="https://symfony.com/bundles/ux-icons/current/index.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Symfony UX Icons&lt;/a&gt;. Et c'est vrai que c'est agréable : une ligne de Twig, n'importe laquelle des plus de 200 000 icônes d'&lt;a href="https://icon-sets.iconify.design/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Iconify&lt;/a&gt;, un &lt;code&gt;ux:icons:lock&lt;/code&gt; avant de déployer, et c'est réglé.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight twig"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="cp"&gt;{{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;ux_icon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'lucide:trash-2'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'text-danger'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'aria-label'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Supprimer'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cp"&gt;}}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Tout va bien. Jusqu'au jour où cette même poubelle doit apparaître dans un contrôleur Stimulus. Ou dans le composant React de la page d'à côté. Là, Twig ne peut plus rien pour vous, et on finit tous par écrire ce genre de joyeuseté :&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// assets/controllers/delete_controller.js&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TRASH_ICON&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&amp;lt;svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="1em" height="1em" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"&amp;gt;&amp;lt;path fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 11v6m4-6v6m5-11v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6M3 6h18M8 6V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h4a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v2"/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/svg&amp;gt;`&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;buttonTarget&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;innerHTML&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TRASH_ICON&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Un SVG copié-collé depuis le navigateur, des attributs recopiés à la main depuis &lt;code&gt;ux_icons.yaml&lt;/code&gt; (ou pas), et un &lt;code&gt;innerHTML&lt;/code&gt; qui fera tiquer votre Content Security Policy. Côté React, c'est &lt;code&gt;lucide-react&lt;/code&gt; qui s'invite dans le &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt; : une deuxième source d'icônes, avec ses propres versions et ses propres attributs par défaut. Et le jour où vous changez &lt;code&gt;default_icon_attributes&lt;/code&gt;, vos icônes Twig changent. Pas les autres. Le fameux "je synchroniserai plus tard".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


L'histoire d'une PR refusée
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mon premier réflexe a été de proposer la fonctionnalité directement à Symfony UX : &lt;a href="https://github.com/symfony/ux/pull/4072" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;symfony/ux#4072&lt;/a&gt;. L'idée : sur le warmup du cache, UX Icons exporte les icônes locales dans un module JavaScript, avec les attributs que &lt;code&gt;ux_icon()&lt;/code&gt; leur donne. Un petit package npm les affiche ensuite en JavaScript, React et Vue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La PR a été fermée. Et pour être honnête, les arguments se tiennent : les bundlers savent déjà importer des &lt;code&gt;.svg&lt;/code&gt; (avec SVGR ou &lt;code&gt;vite-svg-loader&lt;/code&gt;), et l'ajout de React et Vue en dépendances de toutes les applications qui utilisent UX Icons, ce n'était pas un bon deal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;🤓 « &lt;em&gt;Mais alors, SVGR fait déjà le job, non ?&lt;/em&gt; »&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pas tout à fait. SVGR n'a pas vu de release depuis août 2023, et &lt;code&gt;vite-svg-loader&lt;/code&gt; ne connaît que Vite et Vue. Surtout, aucun des deux ne couvre le JavaScript vanilla d'un contrôleur Stimulus. Et aucun ne lit votre config &lt;code&gt;ux_icons&lt;/code&gt; : vos icônes JS n'auront jamais les mêmes attributs que vos icônes Twig.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Le code était écrit, testé, et il me servait. Je l'ai donc sorti en bundle à part, qui se branche sur un UX Icons non modifié. Open source, évidemment : je vous présente &lt;a href="https://github.com/silarhi/ux-icons-js-bundle" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UX Icons JS Bundle&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Et React et Vue y sont des dépendances optionnelles : vous n'installez que ce dont vous vous servez.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Une icône, trois façons de l'afficher
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Le bundle dumpe vos icônes dans &lt;code&gt;var/icons/index.js&lt;/code&gt;, un export nommé par icône. Vous importez celle dont vous avez besoin, comme n'importe quel module :&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// En JavaScript vanilla, par exemple dans un contrôleur Stimulus&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;createIconElement&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@silarhi/ux-icons-js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;LucideTrash2Icon&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../../var/icons/index.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;buttonTarget&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;append&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createIconElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;LucideTrash2Icon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;text-danger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;aria-label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Supprimer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// En React (ou '@silarhi/ux-icons-js/vue' pour Vue)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UXIcon&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@silarhi/ux-icons-js/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;LucideTrash2Icon&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../var/icons/index.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UXIcon&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;icon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;LucideTrash2Icon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;text-danger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;aria&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Supprimer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Et voilà ce que vous obtenez : &lt;strong&gt;exactement le HTML de &lt;code&gt;ux_icon()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;. Pas "à peu près le même". Le même, caractère pour caractère, avec vos &lt;code&gt;default_icon_attributes&lt;/code&gt;, les &lt;code&gt;icon_attributes&lt;/code&gt; de vos icon sets, vos alias et vos suffixes. Le tout sans un seul &lt;code&gt;innerHTML&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La magnifique démo de cet article : 👉 &lt;a href="https://labs.silarhi.fr/icons" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://labs.silarhi.fr/icons&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;En résumé, avant / après :&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Sans UX Icons JS&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Avec UX Icons JS&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source des icônes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;SVG copiés-collés, ou une lib par framework&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Vos icônes UX Icons, et rien d'autre&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Recopiés à la main depuis &lt;code&gt;ux_icons.yaml&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lus depuis la config, comme &lt;code&gt;ux_icon()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JavaScript vanilla&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;innerHTML&lt;/code&gt; et une chaîne de caractères&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;createIconElement()&lt;/code&gt;, sans parser de HTML&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;React / Vue&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;lucide-react&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;@heroicons/vue&lt;/code&gt;…&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Un composant &lt;code&gt;UXIcon&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Taille du bundle&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Ça dépend de la lib&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Seules les icônes importées&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nom d'icône venant d'une API&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tout embarquer, ou un &lt;code&gt;switch&lt;/code&gt; géant&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;loadIcon()&lt;/code&gt; : un chunk par icône&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nouvelle icône&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Télécharger, copier, coller&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Écrire l'import, &lt;code&gt;ux:icons:lock&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


C'est parti
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Deux packages, publiés depuis le même tag git : le bundle Symfony qui dumpe les icônes, et le package npm qui les affiche.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;composer require silarhi/ux-icons-js-bundle
pnpm add @silarhi/ux-icons-js
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Si Flex ne l'a pas fait pour vous, enregistrez le bundle &lt;strong&gt;après&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;UXIconsBundle&lt;/code&gt;, dont il réutilise la configuration :&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight php"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// config/bundles.php&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Symfony\UX\Icons\UXIconsBundle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'all'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Silarhi\UxIconsJsBundle\SilarhiUxIconsJsBundle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'all'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Et c'est tout pour la configuration. Les icônes sont dumpées au prochain warmup du cache, ou à la main pour voir ce qui se passe :&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$ &lt;/span&gt;php bin/console ux-icons-js:dump &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-v&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; lucide:trash-2
&lt;span class="k"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; user

&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;OK] Dumped 2 icon&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;s&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Le dossier &lt;code&gt;var/icons/&lt;/code&gt; est généré : il n'a rien à faire dans git. Si &lt;code&gt;var/&lt;/code&gt; est déjà dans votre &lt;code&gt;.gitignore&lt;/code&gt; (c'est le cas par défaut), vous n'avez rien à faire. Avec AssetMapper, le bundle mappe le dossier tout seul, il ne reste qu'à lui donner un nom dans &lt;code&gt;importmap.php&lt;/code&gt;. Tout est détaillé dans &lt;a href="https://ux-icons-js-bundle.silarhi.dev/php/asset-mapper/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;la doc&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Le plus dur est fait ! &lt;strong&gt;TOP.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Les détails qui m'ont donné du fil à retordre
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Comme souvent, le gros du travail n'est pas là où on l'attend.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Le même HTML, vraiment
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Promettre "le même HTML que &lt;code&gt;ux_icon()&lt;/code&gt;", c'est facile. Le tenir, c'est une autre histoire. Les attributs passés à &lt;code&gt;ux_icon()&lt;/code&gt; suivent les règles de la fonction &lt;a href="https://twig.symfony.com/doc/3.x/functions/html_attr.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;html_attr()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; de Twig, et elles ont leurs subtilités :&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;renderIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;LucideHeartIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// … aria-hidden="true"&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;renderIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;LucideHeartIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;aria-label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Favori&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// … aria-label="Favori"&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;renderIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;LucideHeartIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;btn-icon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;isActive&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;active&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// … class="btn-icon" si isActive est false&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;renderIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;LucideHeartIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// plus de height du tout&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;renderIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;LucideHeartIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;data-config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// … data-config="{&amp;amp;quot;id&amp;amp;quot;:1}"&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;aria-hidden="true"&lt;/code&gt; est ajouté sauf si l'icône a une alternative textuelle, &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; supprime un attribut (même configuré), les tableaux deviennent des listes de classes, les objets des &lt;code&gt;data-*&lt;/code&gt; en JSON… Le côté JavaScript reproduit tout ça, jusqu'à la &lt;strong&gt;position&lt;/strong&gt; des attributs : un attribut redéfini garde sa place dans la balise &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;svg&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, comme en PHP. C'est d'ailleurs un bug que j'avais laissé passer dans la PR, et que le bundle corrige.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pour être sûr de ne pas se raconter d'histoires, les tests comparent la sortie de &lt;code&gt;renderIcon()&lt;/code&gt; à celle de &lt;code&gt;ux_icon()&lt;/code&gt;, octet par octet. La démo le fait aussi, en direct dans votre navigateur.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Un export par icône, pour le tree-shaking
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Chaque icône est un export nommé : le nom de l'icône en PascalCase, suivi de &lt;code&gt;Icon&lt;/code&gt;. Votre bundler ne garde que celles que vous importez, et les autres restent au placard.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Icône&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Export&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;user&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;UserIcon&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;lucide:trash-2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;LucideTrash2Icon&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;fa7-brands:x-twitter&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Fa7BrandsXTwitterIcon&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;500&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;_500Icon&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Petite subtilité : deux icônes peuvent donner le même nom d'export (&lt;code&gt;sub:check&lt;/code&gt; et un alias &lt;code&gt;sub-check&lt;/code&gt; donnent tous les deux &lt;code&gt;SubCheckIcon&lt;/code&gt;). Plutôt que d'en écraser une en silence, le dump échoue et vous donne les deux noms. Une icône qui change toute seule en prod, c'est le genre de bug qu'on met une après-midi à comprendre.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pour TypeScript, un &lt;code&gt;index.d.ts&lt;/code&gt; est dumpé à côté, avec le nom littéral de chaque icône.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Et quand le nom de l'icône vient d'une API ?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;C'est &lt;strong&gt;LE&lt;/strong&gt; cas qui m'a fait sortir une version 0.2.0 dans la foulée. Un import nommé, c'est très bien quand vous connaissez l'icône en écrivant le code. Mais quand votre API renvoie &lt;code&gt;{ "icon": "lucide:server" }&lt;/code&gt;, vous ne la connaissez qu'au runtime. Et embarquer toutes les icônes "au cas où", c'est exactement ce qu'on voulait éviter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Le bundle dumpe donc aussi un &lt;code&gt;loaders.js&lt;/code&gt;, qui associe chaque nom d'icône au module de cette icône seule :&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;createIconElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loadIcon&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@silarhi/ux-icons-js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loaders&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../var/icons/loaders.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/api/status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;icon&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;loadIcon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loaders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;icon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// null pour un nom inconnu&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;icon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;badge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;append&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createIconElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;icon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;text-success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Votre bundler découpe chaque icône dans son propre chunk : importer &lt;code&gt;loaders&lt;/code&gt; ne télécharge aucune icône, et &lt;code&gt;loadIcon()&lt;/code&gt; ne télécharge que celle demandée. Une seule fois, même si dix composants la demandent en même temps. En React et Vue, c'est le composant &lt;code&gt;UXLazyIcon&lt;/code&gt;, avec un fallback pendant le chargement :&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UXLazyIcon&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@silarhi/ux-icons-js/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loaders&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../var/icons/loaders.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UXLazyIcon&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;icon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loaders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loaders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;fallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;placeholder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Et le &lt;code&gt;loaders.d.ts&lt;/code&gt; exporte l'union des noms dumpés, &lt;code&gt;IconName&lt;/code&gt;, pour typer vos réponses d'API ou vos props : une faute de frappe dans un nom d'icône ne passe plus la compilation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


&lt;code&gt;ux:icons:lock&lt;/code&gt;, côté JavaScript
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Avec UX Icons, le workflow classique est d'écrire &lt;code&gt;ux_icon('lucide:mail')&lt;/code&gt; dans un template, puis de lancer &lt;code&gt;ux:icons:lock&lt;/code&gt; : la commande trouve l'icône dans vos templates et la télécharge depuis Iconify. Je voulais exactement la même chose en JavaScript :&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// assets/controllers/mail_controller.js&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;LucideMailIcon&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../../var/icons/index.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$ &lt;/span&gt;php bin/console ux:icons:lock
✓ Imported lucide:mail &lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;License: ISC&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt; Render with: &lt;span class="o"&gt;{{&lt;/span&gt; ux_icon&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'lucide:mail'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;}}&lt;/span&gt;
JavaScript: import &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; LucideMailIcon &lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
// Dumped 3 icon&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;s&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;JavaScript.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Vous écrivez l'import d'une icône qui n'existe pas encore, vous lancez la commande, et elle existe. Le bundle scanne vos fichiers &lt;code&gt;.js&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;.jsx&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;.ts&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;.tsx&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;.vue&lt;/code&gt; et &lt;code&gt;.svelte&lt;/code&gt; à la recherche des imports nommés depuis un module dont le chemin contient &lt;code&gt;icons&lt;/code&gt;, et retrouve le nom de l'icône depuis le nom de l'export. Pas toujours une seule : &lt;code&gt;LucideTrash2Icon&lt;/code&gt; peut venir de &lt;code&gt;lucide:trash-2&lt;/code&gt; ou de &lt;code&gt;lucide:trash2&lt;/code&gt;. Tous les candidats sont proposés à &lt;code&gt;ux:icons:lock&lt;/code&gt;, qui ignore ceux qu'Iconify ne connaît pas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


PHP 8.2 et Symfony 6.4
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La PR visait la dernière version de UX Icons, donc PHP 8.4. Le bundle, lui, descend jusqu'à PHP 8.2, Symfony 6.4 et &lt;code&gt;symfony/ux-icons&lt;/code&gt; 2.36.1 : parce que dans la vraie vie, les projets ne sont pas tous à jour (les miens non plus 🤫). Il y a juste deux limites sur UX Icons 2.x, &lt;code&gt;ux:icons:lock&lt;/code&gt; n'y scanne pas le JavaScript, et les booléens n'y sont pas rendus pareil. Tout est dans &lt;a href="https://ux-icons-js-bundle.silarhi.dev/reference/compatibility/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;les notes de compatibilité&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Ça donne quoi au final ?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La démo de cet article : 👉 &lt;a href="https://labs.silarhi.fr/icons" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://labs.silarhi.fr/icons&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vous y trouverez la même icône rendue par Twig, par JavaScript et par React (avec la comparaison octet par octet), un bouton "copier" en Stimulus qui change d'icône sans &lt;code&gt;innerHTML&lt;/code&gt;, une notation en étoiles en React, et un tableau de statut dont les icônes viennent d'une API : ouvrez l'onglet réseau, chaque icône arrive dans son propre petit chunk. Le code est sur &lt;a href="https://github.com/silarhi/symfony-docker-ci" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;silarhi/symfony-docker-ci&lt;/a&gt;, le projet qui me sert depuis des années pour les démos de ce blog.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pour les curieux, sous le capot :&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PHP 8.2+, Symfony 6.4, 7.x et 8.x, &lt;code&gt;symfony/ux-icons&lt;/code&gt; 2.36.1+ ou 3.5+&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React 18 / 19 et Vue 3 en dépendances optionnelles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Webpack Encore, Vite, AssetMapper : n'importe quel bundler fait l'affaire&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Le corps du SVG est dumpé sous forme d'arbre, React et Vue le rendent en éléments : zéro &lt;code&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/code&gt;, zéro &lt;code&gt;v-html&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100 % du code couvert par les tests, et chaque combinaison de versions testée par la CI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Voilà ! Vos icônes n'ont plus d'excuse pour exister en deux exemplaires. N'hésitez pas à laisser un commentaire si vous l'utilisez, ou si quelque chose coince. Et si le bundle vous fait gagner du temps, une petite ⭐ sur GitHub fait toujours plaisir.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Pour aller plus loin
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://labs.silarhi.fr/icons" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;La démo du tuto&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ux-icons-js-bundle.silarhi.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;La documentation du bundle&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/silarhi/ux-icons-js-bundle" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Le code source du bundle sur GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://packagist.org/packages/silarhi/ux-icons-js-bundle" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Le bundle sur Packagist&lt;/a&gt; et &lt;a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@silarhi/ux-icons-js" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;le package sur npm&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/silarhi/symfony-docker-ci" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Le code source de la démo sur GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/symfony/ux/pull/4072" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;La PR d'origine : symfony/ux#4072&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://symfony.com/bundles/ux-icons/current/index.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;La documentation de Symfony UX Icons&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://blog.silarhi.fr/presentation-picasso-bundle-symfony-image/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;PicassoBundle, le composant image qui manquait à Symfony&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


Fixing Wide Tables on Mobile: Adding Horizontal Scroll without Layout Shift
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I patched the &lt;code&gt;Table&lt;/code&gt; component so that tables wider than the viewport no longer push the page sideways on mobile. The fix adds a responsive wrapper with &lt;code&gt;overflow-x:auto&lt;/code&gt; and a CSS‑only scrollbar, keeping the layout stable while preserving desktop behavior.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our SaaS dashboard renders data‑heavy tables (e.g., contract listings, monthly reports). On a recent QA run on an iPhone 13, the page horizontally scrolled whenever a table exceeded the screen width:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;LayoutError: viewport overflow – element .table-wrapper width 1240px &amp;gt; 375px (mobile)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The symptom was a broken UX: users had to swipe the whole page, and the fixed header disappeared off‑screen. The issue surfaced after PR #24 introduced a new column (&lt;code&gt;tenantId&lt;/code&gt;) that doubled the table width.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first instinct was to force the table to shrink with &lt;code&gt;table-layout: fixed&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;width: 100%&lt;/code&gt;. I added the following CSS directly to &lt;code&gt;Table.jsx&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.table&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;table-layout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fixed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;100%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;On desktop it looked okay, but on mobile the columns collapsed into unreadable ellipses. The real data (IDs, amounts) got truncated, making the table useless. I also tried wrapping the table in a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div class="scroll-container"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;overflow-x: scroll&lt;/code&gt; but forgot to set &lt;code&gt;display: block&lt;/code&gt; on the wrapper, so the scroll area collapsed to zero height. The page still shifted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conclusion: a simple &lt;code&gt;overflow&lt;/code&gt; on the wrapper wasn’t enough; we needed a reliable, responsive container that only activates on small viewports while preserving the existing desktop layout.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Architecture Decision
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I decided to keep the existing &lt;code&gt;Table&lt;/code&gt; component untouched for backward compatibility and introduce a thin wrapper component called &lt;code&gt;ResponsiveTable&lt;/code&gt;. This wrapper:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detects if the table’s natural width exceeds the viewport.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applies a horizontal scroll only on screens ≤ 768 px.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leaves the original table untouched for desktop, avoiding any layout regressions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The wrapper lives in &lt;code&gt;src/components/ResponsiveTable.jsx&lt;/code&gt;. It uses a &lt;code&gt;ref&lt;/code&gt; to measure the table’s scroll width after render and toggles a CSS class accordingly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. New Files
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;File&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Purpose&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;src/components/ResponsiveTable.jsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Wrapper component with resize observer&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;src/styles/responsive-table.css&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CSS for the scrolling container&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;src/components/Table.jsx&lt;/code&gt; (minor import)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Exported as default, now used inside the wrapper&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Code Changes
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;


&lt;code&gt;src/components/ResponsiveTable.jsx&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h4&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Table&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;./Table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;./responsive-table.css&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ResponsiveTableProps&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/**
* Wraps &amp;lt;Table&amp;gt; and adds horizontal scroll on small screens
* when the table’s intrinsic width exceeds the viewport.
*/&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ResponsiveTable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ResponsiveTableProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;wrapperRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;HTMLDivElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tableRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;HTMLTableElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;needsScroll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setNeedsScroll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Measure after mount and on resize&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;observe&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResizeObserver&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;wrapperRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tableRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;wrapperWidth&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;wrapperRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clientWidth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tableWidth&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tableRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;scrollWidth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setNeedsScroll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tableWidth&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;wrapperWidth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;wrapperRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;observe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;observe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;wrapperRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;observe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;disconnect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;wrapperRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`responsive-table-wrapper &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;needsScroll&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;scrollable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;''&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* Pass the ref down so we can measure the real &amp;lt;table&amp;gt; element */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Table&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tableRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Key points:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;ResizeObserver&lt;/strong&gt; – Guarantees the check runs on orientation change or when a user toggles the dev tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;needsScroll&lt;/code&gt; state&lt;/strong&gt; – Toggles the &lt;code&gt;scrollable&lt;/code&gt; class only when necessary, avoiding unnecessary scrollbars on desktop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;ref&lt;/code&gt; forwarding&lt;/strong&gt; – &lt;code&gt;Table.jsx&lt;/code&gt; now exports a forwardRef component.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;


Updating &lt;code&gt;Table.jsx&lt;/code&gt; (only a few lines)
&lt;/h4&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;forwardRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Table&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;forwardRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;HTMLTableElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TableProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"data-table"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;thead&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;tr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;th&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;th&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;tr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;thead&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;tbody&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;row&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;tr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;td&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;row&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;col&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;td&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;tr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;tbody&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;No visual changes; we only expose the underlying &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;table&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; for measurement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;


&lt;code&gt;src/styles/responsive-table.css&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h4&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.responsive-table-wrapper&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;100%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c"&gt;/* Prevent vertical overflow on mobile */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;overflow-y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;hidden&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c"&gt;/* Only enable horizontal scrolling when the class is added */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.responsive-table-wrapper.scrollable&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;overflow-x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;auto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;-webkit-overflow-scrolling&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;touch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c"&gt;/* smooth scrolling on iOS */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c"&gt;/* Optional: hide native scrollbar on WebKit while keeping scrollability */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.responsive-table-wrapper.scrollable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;::-webkit-scrollbar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;6px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.responsive-table-wrapper.scrollable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;background-color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rgba&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;0.2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;border-radius&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;3px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c"&gt;/* Preserve desktop layout */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;@media&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;min-width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;769px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.responsive-table-wrapper&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;overflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;visible&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cp"&gt;!important&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


4. Integration
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the pages that previously imported &lt;code&gt;Table&lt;/code&gt; directly (e.g., &lt;code&gt;src/pages/Contracts.jsx&lt;/code&gt;), I swapped the import:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Before&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Table&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../components/Table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// After&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ResponsiveTable&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../components/ResponsiveTable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;And updated the JSX:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResponsiveTable&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;contracts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;contractColumns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;All other props remained unchanged, so no further refactoring was needed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


5. Testing the Fix
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I added a Cypress test (&lt;code&gt;cypress/integration/table_responsive.spec.js&lt;/code&gt;) that forces a viewport width of 375 px and asserts that the wrapper has the &lt;code&gt;scrollable&lt;/code&gt; class when the table contains more than 8 columns.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;describe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Responsive Table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;adds horizontal scroll on mobile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;viewport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;375&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;667&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;visit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/contracts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;.responsive-table-wrapper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;should&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;have.class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;scrollable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;have.css&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;overflow-x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;auto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;All CI pipelines now pass, and manual testing on iOS Safari confirms the page no longer shifts sideways.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Key Takeaway
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When dealing with wide tables on responsive layouts, isolate the scrolling logic in a dedicated wrapper that &lt;strong&gt;measures&lt;/strong&gt; the table’s intrinsic width rather than relying on static CSS breakpoints. This pattern keeps the desktop experience untouched and only adds scroll when it’s truly needed, avoiding layout shift and preserving accessibility.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What's Next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Lazy‑load column data&lt;/strong&gt; – For tables with &amp;gt; 50 columns, fetch column definitions on demand to reduce initial payload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Keyboard navigation&lt;/strong&gt; – Ensure the scrollable wrapper is focusable (&lt;code&gt;tabindex="0"&lt;/code&gt;) so keyboard users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part of my &lt;a href="https://dev.to/zaerohell"&gt;Build in Public&lt;/a&gt; series — sharing the real process of building Building PlayaMXCRM from Playa del Carmen, México.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Repo: &lt;code&gt;zaerohell/VS&lt;/code&gt; · 2026-10-19&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;#playadev #buildinpublic&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How many times have you felt stuck in your career, like nothing new happens? Perhaps you have worked in the same position for a long time, have not improved your skill set, and cannot see what path your career will take next. Does it remind you of something?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When you feel like you are stuck in your tech career, it is pretty discouraging because it can be difficult to find the right path when working in the IT sphere due to constant changes. However, as I found during my career path, feeling stuck does not always mean you are in the wrong sphere of business; you need a change sometimes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here are 6 steps you should follow in order to find what to do when you feel stuck in your tech career.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. Understand Why You Are Stuck
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To make a step forward in your career, understand why you feel you are stuck.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ask yourself questions like:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are you growing as a professional working in your current position?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is your job interesting to you?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can you be promoted inside the company where you are working?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are your contributions appreciated in the company?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are you burnt out or are you just bored with your work?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Feeling stuck because of burnout and the feeling you have outgrown your current job are not the same thing. For example, if you love software development and your work seems to be repetitive, you should find a new challenge instead of making a turn in another direction. Finding the reason for your feeling can help you find the solutions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. Decide What You Want to Have Next in Your Career
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Another very common mistake is telling you don't want to do something, instead of trying to understand what you do want to do. "It's time for me to have a new job" is easier to say than understanding why you need it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;During my career path, I moved from developer to team lead, then to lead developer, and finally became a technology leader. I couldn't plan my 10-year perspective from the beginning of my career, so I took all steps that could offer me a new experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now, you should not understand your entire future path in detail. Try to define your goals in the near future. Perhaps, it means becoming a senior developer, taking a managerial position, working in DevOps, or some other area. What is more important, now you should think about the next step in your career, not about the entire future path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. Find Out What Additional Skills You Need To Reach Your Objectives
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After having decided on your next step in your career, think about the additional skills you need in order to get to the next level. For example, if you dream about being the technical lead, improving your coding skills is not enough.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The additional skills can be, among others:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explaining complicated technical concepts to specialists in other fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentoring junior developers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Making architectural decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritizing tasks and coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Or, for instance, if your dream is to become a cloud engineer or DevOps specialist, you will need to learn new technologies like Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD pipelines, and cloud platforms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Obviously, you shouldn't learn everything at once. Take one or two skills that would help you come one step closer to your objectives.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. Find Ways to Move Forward With Your Current Employer
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sometimes the best option to break through your feeling of being stuck is to stay where you are and use all existing opportunities. Before you start your job search, you should analyze your current employer and see what opportunities are possible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do you have opportunities to do some volunteering outside your routine tasks? Can you help your junior developers to become better? Are you able to run a small tech project? Discuss your opportunities to develop with your manager.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, if you dream about becoming a lead developer, you can volunteer to manage a small project and lead all technical discussions. All these activities can increase your confidence and show that you are ready for new responsibilities. Of course, every company can offer such opportunities. In case you discussed your goals with your employer but there is no place for you, you can move forward in another way.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


5. Talk to Somebody Who Has Already Had the Same Problems
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Being stuck can blind you and prevent you from noticing some obvious opportunities. Speaking to somebody who had the same experience can help you. Discuss your problems and obstacles with your mentor, former colleagues, or career coach. Tell them about your situation, your goals, and difficulties, and ask them what helped you overcome the mentioned issues.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a career coach for IT professionals, I often observe that people underestimate their experience and abilities. Discussing the issue with somebody else opens new opportunities for you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You do not have to solve everything alone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


6. Make an Action Plan and Start Realizing It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can consider changing your career for a month and do nothing. Making the action plan instead of waiting for a perfect plan can help you start acting.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you want to be a leader, you can schedule a meeting with your manager. If you dream about working with some new technologies, develop a project for yourself. And if you are ready to make applications for new jobs, update your CV and LinkedIn.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Create some achievable goals for the next 30 days and plan the steps.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Ready to Get Your Career Moving?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In case you are feeling stuck, not quite understand how to move forward, or need to make some advances in your career, I can help. Together we will analyze your goals and obstacles, and find some ways to move forward.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://hoffstech.com/coaching" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Book Your Free Career Coaching Consultation!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


From Natural Language to Type-Safe SQL in Java with Querier AI
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What if users could ask questions about their application data in plain English instead of writing SQL or navigating complex filters?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Show me the top 10 customers by total revenue in the last 30 days.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I recently released &lt;strong&gt;Querier AI&lt;/strong&gt;, an optional module of my open-source Java SQL query builder, &lt;a href="https://github.com/AytmaTech/Querier" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Querier&lt;/a&gt;. It translates natural-language prompts into validated Querier &lt;code&gt;Select&lt;/code&gt; objects, allowing you to use AI-powered queries without handing database access directly to an AI model.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this tutorial, we'll integrate it into a Spring Boot application and execute the resulting query using Spring JDBC.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What we're building
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The request flow is straightforward:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A user submits a natural-language question.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Querier AI generates SQL based on the schema you expose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The SQL is validated against that schema and parsed into a Querier &lt;code&gt;Select&lt;/code&gt; object.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your application executes the resulting query through its existing database layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The application displays the results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The important distinction is that the result of the AI operation is a Querier object that your Java application can inspect and use, rather than simply a SQL string to execute blindly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. Add the dependency
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Querier AI is an optional module, so you don't need to add AI dependencies if you only want to use the core query builder.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For Maven, add &lt;code&gt;querier-ai&lt;/code&gt; to your &lt;code&gt;pom.xml&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight xml"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;dependency&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;groupId&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;com.aytmatech&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/groupId&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;artifactId&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;querier-ai&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/artifactId&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;version&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;2.0.0&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/version&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/dependency&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This example uses Querier 2.0.0. Check the &lt;a href="https://github.com/AytmaTech/Querier/releases" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub releases&lt;/a&gt; for newer versions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You'll need Java 17 or higher, a Spring application with database access, and entity classes that describe the tables you want to query.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. Configure your AI endpoint
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Querier AI follows a bring-your-own-key approach. It works with OpenAI-compatible endpoints, including OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, Mistral, and Ollama-compatible setups.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Configure the provider through environment variables rather than hardcoding credentials in your source code:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;export &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;QUERIER_AI_API_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"your-api-key"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;export &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;QUERIER_AI_BASE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://api.openai.com/v1"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;export &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;QUERIER_AI_MODEL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"gpt-4o-mini"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Use the appropriate base URL, model or deployment identifier, and credentials for your provider.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Next, register the AI client and &lt;code&gt;QuerierAi&lt;/code&gt; service as Spring beans:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;com.aytmatech.querier.ai.AiClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;com.aytmatech.querier.ai.QuerierAi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;com.aytmatech.querier.ai.retry.RetryPolicy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@Configuration&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;QuerierAiConfig&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@Bean&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AiClient&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;aiClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AiClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;getenv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"QUERIER_AI_API_KEY"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;baseUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;getenv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"QUERIER_AI_BASE_URL"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;getenv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"QUERIER_AI_MODEL"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@Bean&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;QuerierAi&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;querierAi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AiClient&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;aiClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;QuerierAi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;aiClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;retryPolicy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;RetryPolicy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;ofMaxAttempts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The retry policy allows Querier AI to attempt corrections when generated SQL is invalid. You can adjust the policy to suit your application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep API keys out of logs, source control, and client-side code. In production, use your deployment platform's secret-management facilities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. Choose which entities the AI can see
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The schema you expose is an important part of this integration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suppose your application has &lt;code&gt;Order&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Customer&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;Product&lt;/code&gt; entity classes. You can restrict the AI's schema context to those classes:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;final&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;?&amp;gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;EXPOSED_ENTITIES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Order&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Customer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The first class is treated as the primary entity by the inspector, so put your main entity first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Querier AI can inspect the exposed classes and their mappings to build the schema context:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;com.aytmatech.querier.ai.model.AiSchemaContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;com.aytmatech.querier.ai.model.AiSchemaInspector&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AiSchemaContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;schemaContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AiSchemaInspector&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;inspect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;EXPOSED_ENTITIES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Make sure your entity mappings correctly describe your database schema. Querier supports its own table and column annotations, as well as supported JPA annotations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can also add semantic descriptions and synonyms to help the AI understand domain-specific terms such as "sales," "revenue," or "transactions." See the &lt;a href="https://aytmatech.com/projects/querier/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Querier documentation&lt;/a&gt; for more details.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. Turn a prompt into a validated query
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's implement the core of a Spring MVC controller.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The controller accepts a prompt, creates a &lt;code&gt;QueryRequest&lt;/code&gt;, and sends it to &lt;code&gt;QuerierAi.query()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight java"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;com.aytmatech.querier.Select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;com.aytmatech.querier.ai.QuerierAi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;com.aytmatech.querier.ai.model.AiSchemaContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;com.aytmatech.querier.ai.model.AiSchemaInspector&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;com.aytmatech.querier.ai.query.QueryRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;com.aytmatech.querier.ai.query.QueryResult&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;org.springframework.jdbc.core.namedparam.NamedParameterJdbcTemplate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;org.springframework.stereotype.Controller&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;org.springframework.ui.Model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.PostMapping&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestMapping&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestParam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;java.util.ArrayList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;java.util.LinkedHashSet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;java.util.List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;java.util.Map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@Controller&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@RequestMapping&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/ai"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AiQueryController&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;final&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;?&amp;gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;EXPOSED_ENTITIES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Order&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Customer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;final&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;QuerierAi&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;querierAi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;final&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;NamedParameterJdbcTemplate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;jdbc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;AiQueryController&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;QuerierAi&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;querierAi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;NamedParameterJdbcTemplate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;jdbc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;querierAi&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;querierAi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;jdbc&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;jdbc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@PostMapping&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/query"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@RequestParam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"prompt"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;prompt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Model&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;addAttribute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"queryPrompt"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;prompt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AiSchemaContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;schemaContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AiSchemaInspector&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;inspect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;EXPOSED_ENTITIES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;QueryRequest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;QueryRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;prompt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;prompt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;schemaContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;schemaContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;temperature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;QueryResult&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;querierAi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;(!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;isValid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;addAttribute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s"&gt;"queryError"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"\n"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;validationIssues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;()));&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;interpretationNote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;ifPresent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;note&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;addAttribute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"queryNote"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;note&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;"ai/index"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Select&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;orElseThrow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;SqlAndParams&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sqlAndParams&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;toSqlAndParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;jdbc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;queryForList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;sqlAndParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;sql&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;sqlAndParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ArrayList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;(!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;isEmpty&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;addAll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;LinkedHashSet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;keySet&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;()));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;interpretationNote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;ifPresent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;note&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;addAttribute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"queryNote"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;note&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;addAttribute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"queryColumns"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;addAttribute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"queryRows"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;"ai/index"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is the query endpoint; you'll also need a GET handler or another route to display the initial page. The example assumes your application has the entity classes and a Thymeleaf template at &lt;code&gt;ai/index.html&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A few details are worth highlighting:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;temperature(0.0)&lt;/code&gt; requests a low-variation response for this query-generation flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;result.isValid()&lt;/code&gt; lets you handle validation failures before execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;result.query()&lt;/code&gt; provides the validated &lt;code&gt;Select&lt;/code&gt; object.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;toSqlAndParams()&lt;/code&gt; returns the SQL and named parameters in a form that works with &lt;code&gt;NamedParameterJdbcTemplate&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The controller also makes an interpretation note available to the view when Querier AI provides one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


5. Add a simple form and results table
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You don't need a special frontend framework to try this feature. A basic Thymeleaf form is enough:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;form&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;method=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"post"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;th:action=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"@{/ai/query}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;textarea&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"prompt"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;placeholder=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Show the top 10 customers by revenue in the last 30 days"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/textarea&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"submit"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Run query&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/form&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If Spring Security is enabled, make sure your form includes the appropriate CSRF protection.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To display validation errors:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;th:if=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"${queryError}"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;class=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"alert alert-error"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;strong&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Could not generate a valid query:&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/strong&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;pre&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;th:text=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"${queryError}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/pre&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;And to render the result rows dynamically:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;table&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;th:if=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"${queryColumns != null and !queryColumns.isEmpty()}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;thead&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;tr&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;th&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;th:each=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"column : ${queryColumns}"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;th:text=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"${column}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/th&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/tr&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/thead&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;tbody&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;tr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;th:each=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"row : ${queryRows}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;td&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;th:each=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"column : ${queryColumns}"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;th:text=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"${row.get(column)}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/td&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/tr&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/tbody&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/table&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The column names and row values are derived from the query result, so the same template can display different query shapes. In a complete application, add a separate empty-state message for successful queries that return zero rows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


6. What about security?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Validating the generated query against the exposed schema is an important safeguard, but it shouldn't replace your application's normal security controls.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before using this in production:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expose only the entities and columns that the feature should be able to query.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use a database account with the minimum privileges necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply user authorization, tenant isolation, query timeouts, and sensible result-size limits in your application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Don't assume that a valid query is automatically authorized for every user.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be careful about exposing generated SQL or database details to end users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your application remains responsible for deciding which data a user may access and for executing the query safely.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Try Querier AI
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can now take a natural-language question, convert it into a validated Querier &lt;code&gt;Select&lt;/code&gt;, and execute it through the database layer you already use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The AI module is optional, and the rest of Querier remains a Java query-building library.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Explore the project and source code:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/AytmaTech/Querier" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Querier on GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://aytmatech.com/projects/querier/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Querier documentation and quick start&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the next tutorial, we'll use the same AI integration to generate an entire dashboard from one natural-language description.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Autonomous robots, drones, and vehicles can perform tasks independently. Coordinating them as a fleet, however, introduces a different engineering challenge: every platform must complete its assigned work without creating conflicts with other platforms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider an industrial operation where a drone inspects an elevated structure, a ground robot checks equipment, and an autonomous vehicle delivers materials. Each platform has its own capabilities, navigation requirements, and operating constraints. Yet their missions may depend on shared routes, resource availability, and successful handovers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is where mixed fleet coordination becomes important. Rather than treating every autonomous machine as an isolated system, fleet-level planning manages the dependencies between their tasks while preserving local autonomy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Why Independent Autonomy Is Not Enough&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An individual robot can navigate its environment successfully and still contribute to an inefficient overall operation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, two robots may reserve the same narrow passage, a delivery vehicle may arrive before a receiving operation is ready, or a drone inspection may remain incomplete after a communication interruption.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These problems are not necessarily failures of the individual platforms. They arise because the platforms share resources and depend on one another's activities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A fleet coordination layer can manage several responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Assigning missions according to platform capability and availability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Coordinating shared routes and resource reservations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tracking task progress and completion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Managing charging requirements and mission handovers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reassigning incomplete tasks after a platform failure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Maintaining consistent fleet-level state as conditions change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The goal is to improve the performance of the entire operation rather than optimize each platform independently.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design Task Assignment Around Capabilities and Dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Task allocation should consider more than which platform is available first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A mission may require a particular sensor, payload, operating range, location, or energy reserve. It may also depend on another task being completed before work can begin.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A useful task record includes:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A unique task identifier.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The mission objective and location.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Required platform capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Current assignment and task status.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Dependencies on other tasks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Relevant resource reservations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Completion or verification requirements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider a simple sequence in which a drone inspects an elevated structure, a ground robot examines an accessible area, and a vehicle delivers materials to a designated location.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fleet planner must determine whether these missions can run concurrently or whether one depends on another. It should also distinguish between a task being assigned, started, completed, and verified.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without these distinctions, the system can mistakenly treat an incomplete mission as finished or assign the same work to multiple platforms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prevent Route Conflicts and Resource Deadlocks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Shared environments introduce coordination problems that individual path planners cannot always resolve independently.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A robot may need a corridor that another platform has already reserved. A delivery vehicle may occupy a loading area longer than expected. Multiple robots may also require access to the same charging station.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One approach is to combine fleet-level scheduling with time-bounded resource reservations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, a platform can reserve a shared passage for a defined interval. Other platforms can schedule their movements around that reservation. If the first platform is delayed, the reservation may need to be updated so that the rest of the fleet does not continue operating on outdated assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Deadlock prevention requires additional care. Two platforms can each wait for a resource held by the other, leaving neither able to proceed. Resource ordering, reservation policies, timeout handling, and recovery procedures can help reduce this risk.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These mechanisms should be evaluated against the actual environment. A strategy that works in a wide warehouse may not be appropriate for a narrow industrial corridor or an environment shared by aerial and ground platforms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recover From Failures Without Duplicating Work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failure recovery is one of the most important tests of a coordination system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine that a drone begins an inspection but becomes unavailable before the mission is confirmed complete. Immediately assigning the same inspection to another drone might appear reasonable, but the original platform's state could be uncertain. It may have completed part of the work, or it may still be operating without a reliable communication link.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A safer reassignment workflow separates confirmed information from assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Step 1: Identify the affected task. Determine which mission is associated with the unavailable platform.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Step 2: Check the last confirmed state. Establish whether the mission is complete, incomplete, canceled, or awaiting verification.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Step 3: Resolve the existing assignment. Before issuing replacement work, update the task record so that the system does not maintain conflicting active assignments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Step 4: Select a suitable replacement. Check platform capabilities, resource availability, location, and energy requirements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Step 5: Revalidate shared resources. Confirm that the replacement mission will not conflict with existing route reservations or other assignments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Step 6: Record the recovery outcome. Track whether the replacement mission was accepted, started, completed, and verified.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This process does not eliminate every failure scenario, but it provides a clearer basis for making reassignment decisions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It also highlights why missing telemetry should not automatically be interpreted as proof of failure. Communication loss creates uncertainty, and the coordination system needs an explicit policy for handling it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Separate Fleet-Level Planning From Local Control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A fleet coordination architecture should distinguish between decisions that affect multiple platforms and decisions that belong to an individual platform.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fleet-level planning can determine mission priorities, task assignments, shared resource reservations, and handover timing. Local controllers handle platform-specific navigation, obstacle avoidance, and protective functions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This separation reduces the need for a central dispatcher to manage every movement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It also matters during network interruptions. A robot should follow its predefined local operating and protective procedures if fleet-level communication becomes unavailable. Depending on its design and operating environment, it may continue a permitted local task, pause, return to a designated state, or request assistance when communication resumes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct response must be defined for the particular system rather than assumed to be the same for every robot or vehicle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Coordination software should not override platform-specific safety requirements simply to keep a fleet schedule on track.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate Coordination With Measurable Outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A successful demonstration should show more than several robots completing their missions under ideal conditions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Simulation provides a controlled way to introduce route conflicts, delayed messages, unavailable resources, and platform failures before connecting physical systems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Useful evaluation metrics include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Metric&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What it measures&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fleet throughput&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tasks completed within a defined period&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Task duplication&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Repeated or conflicting task assignments&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Deadlocks&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Situations in which resource conflicts prevent progress&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Charging availability&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Whether platforms can access charging when needed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Missed handovers&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failed transitions between tasks or platforms&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Outage behavior&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Whether platforms follow their defined local procedures during communication loss&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failure recovery time&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Time required to restore an affected mission or operation&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These metrics should be considered together. Higher throughput is not necessarily an improvement if it comes with more duplicate tasks, failed handovers, or unresolved resource conflicts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Testing should also distinguish simulated outcomes from real-world results. Simulation can reveal weaknesses in task allocation and recovery logic, but physical integration introduces additional communication, sensing, and timing constraints.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start Small and Expand Incrementally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A practical first demonstration can use three mission types: aerial inspection, ground inspection, and material delivery.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Begin with a limited number of simulated platforms and a shared dispatch interface. Record task assignments, resource reservations, state changes, and recovery events. Then introduce controlled failures to test whether the fleet can recover without duplicating tasks or creating additional conflicts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once the coordination logic has been evaluated, available physical platforms can be integrated incrementally.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This approach makes it easier to isolate problems in task scheduling, platform interfaces, and shared-state management before increasing system complexity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Research into mixed fleet coordination and distributed intelligence explores these challenges within the broader field of Physical AI and autonomous logistics.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conclusion&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reliable mixed fleets require more than capable individual robots. They need a coordination layer that manages task dependencies, shared resources, mission state, and recovery when conditions change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The strongest designs distinguish fleet-level planning from local autonomy, treat communication delays as a source of uncertainty, and evaluate performance under both normal and failure conditions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By measuring throughput, task duplication, deadlocks, handovers, and recovery behavior, engineering teams can determine whether coordination genuinely improves the operation. These principles provide a practical starting point for developing more reliable autonomous systems across industrial inspection, logistics, and material handling.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


Automating Multi‑Channel Content Publishing with a Git‑Driven Pipeline
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I built a Git‑hook‑triggered pipeline that reads markdown assets, updates &lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt;, and pushes the same article to Medium, Substack, Bluesky, and Dev.to. The change eliminates manual copy‑pastes and rate‑limit crashes by centralizing content generation in Docker.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our VibeCoding blog lives on several platforms. Every time I wrote a post, I had to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Copy the markdown into Medium’s editor, fix front‑matter, and hit publish.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do the same for Substack, then Bluesky, then Dev.to.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On October 17 2026 the Slack bot that auto‑generates these drafts hit a &lt;strong&gt;rate‑limit panic&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;429 Too Many Requests&lt;/code&gt;) while trying to post to Medium, and the Docker build that bundles the publishing scripts failed with merge‑conflict errors in &lt;code&gt;package-lock.json&lt;/code&gt;. The result was a silent bot and a backlog of unpublished content.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The symptoms were:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error: request to https://api.medium.com/v1/users/.../posts failed, status code 429
Docker build failed: conflict in package-lock.json at line 1123
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;We needed a reliable, single source of truth for content and a way to push it atomically to all destinations.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first attempt was a &lt;strong&gt;bash script&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;publish.sh&lt;/code&gt;) that iterated over a hard‑coded list of platforms:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;#!/usr/bin/env bash&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;platform &lt;span class="k"&gt;in &lt;/span&gt;medium substack devto&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;do
&lt;/span&gt;node publish-&lt;span class="k"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;platform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;.js ./content/&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$DATE&lt;/span&gt;/&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$POST&lt;/span&gt;.md
&lt;span class="k"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Problems:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The script ran sequentially, so a single 429 error halted the whole pipeline.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform‑specific metadata (tags, canonical URLs) was duplicated across scripts, leading to drift.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The script lived outside Docker, so local environment mismatches caused the &lt;code&gt;package-lock.json&lt;/code&gt; merge conflict during CI builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The approach failed fast, confirming that a more robust, declarative system was required.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. File Layout
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;content/
└─ 2026/10/18/
├─ VS/
│   ├─ changelog.md
│   ├─ medium_en.md
│   ├─ medium_es.md
│   ├─ substack_en.md
│   ├─ substack_es.md
│   ├─ bluesky_en.json
│   └─ metadata.json
└─ … (other projects)
scripts/
├─ generate-index.ts
├─ publish.ts
└─ utils/
└─ rateLimiter.ts
Dockerfile
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;All platform‑specific markdown files sit next to a &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; that tracks generation status:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"title"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Next.js Minor Version Bump Felt Like a Roadblock"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"date"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"2026-10-18"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"platforms"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"medium"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"substack"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"bluesky"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"devto"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"pull_requests"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"releases"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"closed_issues"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"medium_generated"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"substack_generated"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(Diff snippet from the commit – note the flag changes)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -14,8 +14,8 @@&lt;/span&gt;
"pull_requests": 0,
"releases": 0,
"closed_issues": 0,
&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-  "medium_generated": false,
-  "substack_generated": false,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  "medium_generated": true,
+  "substack_generated": true,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


2. Docker‑Encapsulated Runner
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The pipeline runs inside a Docker container to guarantee identical Node versions and lockfile integrity.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight docker"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;FROM&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;node:20-alpine&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;WORKDIR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; /app&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;COPY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; package*.json ./&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;RUN &lt;/span&gt;npm ci

&lt;span class="k"&gt;COPY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; . .&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;RUN &lt;/span&gt;npm run build   &lt;span class="c"&gt;# TypeScript compilation&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;FROM&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; node:20-alpine&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;WORKDIR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; /app&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;COPY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; --from=builder /app/dist ./dist&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;COPY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; package*.json ./&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;RUN &lt;/span&gt;npm ci &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--production&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;ENTRYPOINT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; ["node", "dist/publish.js"]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;Dockerfile&lt;/code&gt; ensures the &lt;code&gt;package-lock.json&lt;/code&gt; is generated once (&lt;code&gt;npm ci&lt;/code&gt;) and never conflicts during CI runs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Central Publishing Engine (&lt;code&gt;publish.ts&lt;/code&gt;)
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;readFileSync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;writeFileSync&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;postToMedium&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;./utils/medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;postToSubstack&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;./utils/substack&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;postToBluesky&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;./utils/bluesky&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;postToDevto&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;./utils/devto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rateLimit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;./utils/rateLimiter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Meta&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;platforms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Record&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;publish&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;postDir&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;metaPath&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;postDir&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;metadata.json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Meta&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;parse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;readFileSync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;metaPath&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;utf8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tasks&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;postToMedium&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;substack&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;postToSubstack&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;bluesky&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;postToBluesky&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;devto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;postToDevto&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tasks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;platforms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`✅ &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; already published`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;continue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;readFileSync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;postDir&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;_en.md`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;utf8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;rateLimit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;platforms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`🚀 Published to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`❌ Failed &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;:`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Do not abort; continue with other platforms&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;writeFileSync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;metaPath&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Entry point – receives the directory via env var set by CI&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;postDir&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;POST_DIR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;publish&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;postDir&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Key points:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Rate limiting&lt;/strong&gt; is abstracted in &lt;code&gt;rateLimiter.ts&lt;/code&gt;, which uses an exponential back‑off strategy per platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The script reads the per‑platform markdown (&lt;code&gt;medium_en.md&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;substack_en.md&lt;/code&gt;, etc.) and posts them via dedicated helpers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After a successful post, the &lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt; flag is flipped, making the operation idempotent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


4. Rate Limiter (&lt;code&gt;rateLimiter.ts&lt;/code&gt;)
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
